  "summary": "The FlexLine TS03 is Leica's classic manual total station: a proven instrument for the survey and layout work that fills the week, without the complexity of a robotic setup. It runs Leica FlexField software onboard, so most survey and stakeout tasks are carried out without leaving the instrument.\n\nAngular accuracy is available in 2, 3 and 5 second versions, with prism range from 0.9 m to 3,500 m and non-prism measurement over any surface to 500 m. Endless drives in both axes, a user-definable trigger key and pinpoint EDM keep the points coming.\n\nIt is built to be worked hard: IP66, -20 to +50 degrees C, Military Standard 810G and 4.3 kg. LOC8 tracking and theft deterrence can be fitted to keep an eye on the instrument while it is out on site.",
  "specs": [
    "Angular accuracy 2, 3 and 5 seconds (absolute, continuous, diametrical), display resolution 0.1 seconds",
    "Prism range (GPR1, GPH1P) 0.9 m to 3,500 m; GPR1 long range mode over 10,000 m",
    "Non-prism over any surface to 500 m: 2 mm + 2 ppm, typically 2.4 s (R1000 not available on this model)",
    "Single prism 1 mm + 1.5 ppm, typically 2.4 s; tracking 3 mm + 1.5 ppm, typically under 0.15 s",
    "Quadruple axis compensation, compensator range +/- 4 minutes, setting accuracy 0.5 / 1 / 1.5 / 2 seconds",
    "30x telescope, focus 1.55 m to infinity, 3 second resolving power",
    "3.5-inch QVGA grayscale display with 28 keys; endless drives and a user-definable trigger key",
    "Operating time up to 30 hours with the GEB361 battery",
    "4 GB internal memory, SD card and USB memory stick; RS232 and USB interfaces",
    "IP66, -20 to +50 degrees C, Military Standard 810G, 4.3 kg",
    "LOC8 tracking and theft deterrence device available as an option",
    "Leica FlexField software onboard"
  ],
